      "title": "About this workflow",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Bundle Library example\n\nThe **Load Bundle** node gives the Z-Image Turbo subgraph a prompt (`text`), a starting picture (`image`), `steps`,\n`denoise`, and whether to start from that picture (`i2i`).\n\n1. Get the example bundles: open Bundle Library (the box in the sidebar, then **Open library**). In an empty library,\n   click **Import the examples**. A library with bundles already can import `web/examples/example-bundles.zip` from\n   the node pack with the import button.\n2. Choose a bundle on the Load Bundle node and run. Choose another and run again: the same workflow makes that\n   bundle's picture.\n\nThe example bundles have the same five fields, so the links stay as they are when you switch.\n\nProblems with this example: [Bundle Library issues](https://github.com/romanyogurt/ComfyUI-Bundle-Library/issues)\n\n## Model links\n\nFrom Comfy-Org's Z-Image Turbo template ([workflow_templates](https://github.com/Comfy-Org/workflow_templates),\nMIT License, Copyright (c) 2023-present Comfy Org).\n\n- [Hugging Face: Comfy-Org/z_image_turbo](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/z_image_turbo)\n- [ModelScope: Comfy-Org/z_image_turbo](https://modelscope.cn/models/Comfy-Org/z_image_turbo)\n\n**text_encoders**\n\n- [qwen_3_4b.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/z_image_turbo/resolve/main/split_files/text_encoders/qwen_3_4b.safetensors) (7.49 GB)\n\n**diffusion_models**\n\n- [z_image_turbo_bf16.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/z_image_turbo/resolve/main/split_files/diffusion_models/z_image_turbo_bf16.safetensors) (11.46 GB)\n\n**vae**\n\n- [ae.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/z_image_turbo/resolve/main/split_files/vae/ae.safetensors) (319.8 MB)\n\n\nModel Storage Location\n\n```\n📂 ComfyUI/\n├── 📂 models/\n│   ├── 📂 text_encoders/\n│   │      └── qwen_3_4b.safetensors\n│   ├── 📂 diffusion_models/\n│   │      └── z_image_turbo_bf16.safetensors\n│   └── 📂 vae/\n│          └── ae.safetensors\n```\n"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## Bundle Library example\n\nThe **Load Bundle** node gives the Z-Image Turbo subgraph a prompt (`text`), a starting picture (`image`), `steps`,\n`denoise`, and whether to start from that picture (`i2i`).\n\n1. Get the example bundles: open Bundle Library (the box in the sidebar, then **Open library**). In an empty library,\n   click **Import the examples**. A library with bundles already can import `web/examples/example-bundles.zip` from\n   the node pack with the import button.\n2. Choose a bundle on the Load Bundle node and run. Choose another and run again: the same workflow makes that\n   bundle's picture.\n\nThe example bundles have the same five fields, so the links stay as they are when you switch.\n\nProblems with this example: [Bundle Library issues](https://github.com/romanyogurt/ComfyUI-Bundle-Library/issues)\n\n## Model links\n\nFrom Comfy-Org's Z-Image Turbo template ([workflow_templates](https://github.com/Comfy-Org/workflow_templates),\nMIT License, Copyright (c) 2023-present Comfy Org).\n\n- [Hugging Face: Comfy-Org/z_image_turbo](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/z_image_turbo)\n- [ModelScope: Comfy-Org/z_image_turbo](https://modelscope.cn/models/Comfy-Org/z_image_turbo)\n\n**text_encoders**\n\n- [qwen_3_4b.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/z_image_turbo/resolve/main/split_files/text_encoders/qwen_3_4b.safetensors) (7.49 GB)\n\n**diffusion_models**\n\n- [z_image_turbo_bf16.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/z_image_turbo/resolve/main/split_files/diffusion_models/z_image_turbo_bf16.safetensors) (11.46 GB)\n\n**vae**\n\n- [ae.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/z_image_turbo/resolve/main/split_files/vae/ae.safetensors) (319.8 MB)\n\n\nModel Storage Location\n\n```\n📂 ComfyUI/\n├── 📂 models/\n│   ├── 📂 text_encoders/\n│   │      └── qwen_3_4b.safetensors\n│   ├── 📂 diffusion_models/\n│   │      └── z_image_turbo_bf16.safetensors\n│   └── 📂 vae/\n│          └── ae.safetensors\n```\n"
      },
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    },
